    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d214">

                <pb facs="0326" n="1080" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v02/pg1080"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 658.119/109b</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-12-03T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 3, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>430. After consultation with McCormick it has been decided negotiations of agreement with
                    Sweden should be carried on in London. McCormick returning from Paris
                    this week to take up this question with British and French and will try to reach
                    some understanding.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
